.TH BUILDTOOL 1 "September 2026" GNUstep "GNUstep System Manual"
.SH NAME
buildtool \- build and translate Xcode projects with GNUstep
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B buildtool
.RI " [options] [build | clean | install | link]"
.P
.B buildtool
.RI " [options] generate"
.I generator
.P
.B buildtool
.RI " [options] save"
.I output_directory
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B buildtool
utility is the command-line front end for the GNUstep XCode library. It reads
Xcode project files and workspaces, interprets their targets, build
configurations, dependencies, and build phases, and then performs a build-like
operation on GNUstep systems.
.PP
The default operation is
.BR build .
If no operation is specified,
.B buildtool
searches the current working directory for an
.I .xcworkspace
bundle first, then for an
.I .xcodeproj
bundle, and builds the first matching entry it finds. Hidden AppleDouble files
whose names contain
.I ._
are ignored during this search.
.PP
For an Xcode project,
.B buildtool
loads
.I project.pbxproj
from the project bundle. For a workspace, it loads
.I contents.xcworkspacedata
from the workspace bundle and visits the referenced projects in reverse
workspace order. Workspace builds collect library, link, and include paths from
the referenced projects and pass them into each project build.
.PP
Build products are written below the current directory, normally as:
.PP
.RS
.I build/TARGET_NAME/Products/PRODUCT_NAME
.RE
.PP
Applications and bundles are laid out as product wrappers. Framework targets
receive a framework directory structure with
.I Versions
and compatibility symlinks. Generated headers for frameworks and libraries may
be placed below
.IR derived_src .
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.B build
Build the selected project or workspace. This is the default operation. Project
builds apply the selected configuration, plan target order, build target
dependencies, create product directories, and execute each target's build
phases.
.TP
.B clean
Clean the selected project or workspace. Project targets remove their
.I build/TARGET_NAME
directory and remove
.I derived_src
when present.
.TP
.B install
Install previously built products into GNUstep local installation directories.
Tools are copied to the directory reported by
.BR "gnustep-config --variable=GNUSTEP_LOCAL_TOOLS" .
Applications are copied to
.BR GNUSTEP_LOCAL_APPS .
Frameworks are copied under
.BR GNUSTEP_LOCAL_LIBRARY/Frameworks ,
with Headers and Libraries symlinks created under the GNUstep local library
tree. Static and dynamic libraries are copied to the corresponding GNUstep
local library locations and generated headers are installed below
.BR GNUSTEP_LOCAL_HEADERS .
.TP
.B link
Run only the link stage for supported targets. This is mainly useful after
object files have already been built or when debugging link behavior.
.TP
.BI "generate " generator
Translate the selected project using a generator bundle. The generator name is
lower-cased and loaded as
.IB generator .generator
from the user's, local, or system GNUstep
.I Library/Bundles
directories. The source tree includes generator bundles named
.BR makefile ,
.BR cmake ,
.BR projectbuilder ,
and
.BR projectcenter .
For example,
.I buildtool generate makefile
uses
.IR makefile.generator .
.TP
.BI "save " output_directory
Re-archive the parsed Xcode project into
.I output_directory/project.pbxproj
using the current libs-xcode object model. The output directory is created if
needed. This operation is for inspecting or rewriting the parsed project, not
for producing a complete
.I .xcodeproj
bundle by itself.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-project " path
Use the specified Xcode project. The path may name an
.I .xcodeproj
bundle or a
.I project.pbxproj
file. If the path is not recognized,
.B buildtool
falls back to searching the current directory.
.TP
.BI "\-workspace " path
Use the specified Xcode workspace. The path may name an
.I .xcworkspace
bundle or a
.I contents.xcworkspacedata
file. If the path is not recognized,
.B buildtool
falls back to searching the current directory.
.TP
.BI "\-target " name
Restrict a project operation to targets whose name exactly matches
.IR name .
If no matching target exists, the operation is not run.
.TP
.BI "\-scheme " name
Accepted as a target-name alias when
.B \-target
is not supplied. It does not currently interpret Xcode scheme files.
.TP
.BI "\-configuration " name
Set the default build configuration name on the project and on every selected
target before running the operation.
.TP
.B \-alltargets
Build all targets even when
.B \-target
or
.B \-scheme
is supplied.
.TP
.BI "\-sdk " sdk
Accepted for command-line compatibility with
.BR xcodebuild .
The current command-line front end parses the value but does not otherwise
apply it.
.TP
.BI "\-arch " arch
Accepted for
.B xcodebuild
compatibility. The current command-line front end parses the value but does not
otherwise apply it.
.TP
.BI "\-destination " destination
Accepted for
.B xcodebuild
compatibility. The current command-line front end parses the value but does not
otherwise apply it.
.TP
.BI "\-derivedDataPath " path
Accepted for
.B xcodebuild
compatibility. Build products still use the GNUstep build layout described
above.
.TP
.BI "\-archivePath " path
Accepted for
.B xcodebuild
compatibility. Archive creation is not currently implemented by this front end.
.TP
.BI "\-jobs " count
Accepted for
.B xcodebuild
compatibility. Parallel source builds are controlled by
.I buildtool.plist
rather than this option.
.TP
.B \-parallelizeTargets
Accepted for
.B xcodebuild
compatibility.
.TP
.B \-quiet
Accepted for
.B xcodebuild
compatibility.
.TP
.B \-verbose
Accepted for
.B xcodebuild
compatibility.
.TP
.B \-list
Accepted for
.B xcodebuild
compatibility.
.TP
.B \-showBuildSettings
Accepted for
.B xcodebuild
compatibility.
.TP
.B \-license
Accepted for
.B xcodebuild
compatibility.
.TP
.BI "\-write " path
Parsed as an option that takes a value. In the current implementation it records
the requested path and suppresses normal build operations; no output writer is
implemented.
.SH PROJECT SELECTION
When neither
.B \-project
nor
.B \-workspace
is supplied,
.B buildtool
examines only the current working directory. It does not recursively search
parent or child directories.
.PP
If both
.B \-project
and
.B \-workspace
are supplied,
.B \-workspace
takes precedence. In normal use, specify only one.
.PP
Bare positional project filenames are not part of the current interface. Use
.B \-project
or
.B \-workspace
to select a project or workspace explicitly.
.SH BUILDTOOL.PLIST
If a file named
.I buildtool.plist
exists in the current directory, the XCode library reads it as an additional
configuration file. Top-level keys apply globally. A dictionary whose key is a
target name may override or extend the global settings for that target.
.PP
Recognized settings include:
.TP
.B target
Select platform-specific behavior. Common values documented by the project are
.BR msvc ,
.BR linux ,
and
.BR msys2 .
.TP
.B setupScript
Shell script used to prepare the command environment before compiler or shell
commands are run.
.TP
.B buildType
Select source build scheduling. Documented values are
.B linear
and
.BR parallel .
.TP
.B cpus
Number of CPUs to use for parallel source builds.
.TP
.B copylibs
When set to
.BR YES ,
copy shared libraries into the application or bundle product when supported.
.TP
.B ignored
Array of frameworks or libraries to omit from link commands.
.TP
.B headerPaths
Array of additional include paths used while compiling source files.
.TP
.B remappedSource
Dictionary mapping an Xcode source filename to an alternate source filename.
This is useful for substituting GNUstep-specific source files.
.TP
.B skippedTarget
Array of target names to skip during build or link operations.
.TP
.B linkerPaths
Array of additional library search paths. These are emitted as
.B \-L
arguments during linking.
.TP
.B additionalCFlags
Additional C or Objective-C compiler flags.
.TP
.B substitutions
Dictionary of link argument replacements. Mapping a library to the empty string
removes it from the link line.
.TP
.B additional
Array of extra linker arguments to append.
.TP
.B searchReplace
Dictionary of substitutions applied to shell-script build phases.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build the first workspace or project in the current directory:
.PP
.RS
.I buildtool
.RE
.PP
Build a specific project:
.PP
.RS
.I buildtool -project MyApp.xcodeproj
.RE
.PP
Build a specific target and configuration:
.PP
.RS
.I buildtool -project MyApp.xcodeproj -target MyApp -configuration Debug
.RE
.PP
Use a scheme name as a target-name alias:
.PP
.RS
.I buildtool -workspace MyWorkspace.xcworkspace -scheme MyApp
.RE
.PP
Clean a project:
.PP
.RS
.I buildtool -project MyApp.xcodeproj clean
.RE
.PP
Generate a GNUmakefile-oriented project output with the makefile generator:
.PP
.RS
.I buildtool -project MyApp.xcodeproj generate makefile
.RE
.PP
Generate CMake files:
.PP
.RS
.I buildtool -project MyApp.xcodeproj generate cmake
.RE
.PP
Install built products into GNUstep local installation directories:
.PP
.RS
.I buildtool -project MyApp.xcodeproj install
.RE
.PP
Save the parsed project representation:
.PP
.RS
.I buildtool -project MyApp.xcodeproj save NewProject.xcodeproj
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
The current
.B buildtool
main program returns 0 after argument processing completes. Operation failures
are reported in the command output as failed build, clean, install, generate,
link, or save operations rather than through distinct process exit codes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I project.pbxproj
The Xcode project property list read from an
.I .xcodeproj
bundle.
.TP
.I contents.xcworkspacedata
The workspace file read from an
.I .xcworkspace
bundle.
.TP
.I buildtool.plist
Optional per-directory build customization file.
.TP
.I build/
Default build product tree.
.TP
.I derived_src/
Generated source and header tree used by some product types.
.SH BUGS
The command intentionally accepts several
.B xcodebuild
options for compatibility before all corresponding behavior is implemented.
Bare positional project filenames are ignored by the current parser. The
.B \-list
and
.B \-showBuildSettings
options are accepted but do not currently display Xcode-style reports.
.PP
Please report issues on the libs-xcode tracker:
.I https://github.com/gnustep/libs-xcode/issues
.SH HISTORY
.B buildtool
was originally written in August 2011 as part of the GNUstep XCode library
effort and has been updated as libs-xcode gained project, workspace, build, and
generator support.
.PP
This manual page was first written in June 2023 and expanded in September
2026.
